<title>USA: ANTEC sees Q2 hurt by key customer's slowdown.</title>
<headline>ANTEC sees Q2 hurt by key customer's slowdown.</headline>
<dateline>ROLLING MEADOWS, Ill. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANTEC Corp said Thursday it expects financial results in the 1997 second quarter will continue to be hurt by a slowdown in spending by its largest domestic cable customer.</p>
<p>&quot;Sales and earnings will continue to be adversely affected throughout the second quarter by the slowdown in capital spending by our largest customer,&quot; John Egan, ANTEC's chief executive officer and chairman, said in a statement.</p>
<p>The customer was not identified.</p>
</text>
